# Line endings are a property of this repository, not of each contributor's git install.
#
# Every text file is stored LF and checked out LF on every platform. Without this, Git for
# Windows' stock `core.autocrlf=true` checks the tree out CRLF, and the frontend Prettier gate
# (`npm run format:check`, whose `endOfLine` default is `lf`) then reports every file as
# unformatted while CI is green and nothing is actually mis-formatted — issue #636.
#
# `text=auto` decides text-vs-binary by content, so binaries are never converted; the explicit
# `binary` lines below mean the tracked ones do not rely on that heuristic. `platform/.gitattributes`
# sits deeper and so keeps precedence for the files it names (`gradlew`, `*.bat`, `*.jar`).

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts stay LF wherever they run — the cloud-session hooks, and any Linux shell.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binaries: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
